;; The whole vocabulary of this example: one subject. Every step in
;; login.feature is a builtin acting as :user, and this file is what makes
;; :user a known actor (an unknown subject warns at planning time).
;;
;; Discovered automatically — it sits at the conventional path next to
;; shiftlefter.edn, so the config needs no :glossaries key. Example 02b
;; grows this file into a multi-actor glossary (:user/alice, :user/bob).

{:subjects
 {:user {:desc "The one person driving the browser"}}}
